  "* / armed_gate": "FALSE for every hypothesis. armed_gate reads vehicle arming state and elapsed time (online.py:491-496); no monitored sensor channel feeds it. Closure is exogenous.",
  "* / gps_warmup": "FALSE for every hypothesis. Pure elapsed time (ticks > 3.0, comparator.py:199).",
  "gps_fault / gvalid": "TRUE. gvalid is fix validity (comparator.py:115; fix_type >= 3 at ulog_source.py:178). Denial, jamming and many spoofing modes drop or invalidate the fix. The fault silences the gate that carries its own evidence.",
  "gps_fault / speed_gate": "UNKNOWN. speed_gate is computed from GPS-derived horizontal velocity (comparator.py:112-113), so a GPS fault perturbs its input \u2014 but whether it drives the gate CLOSED depends on the spoof's velocity profile, which the fault model does not fix. A spoof holding plausible velocity leaves it open; one collapsing reported velocity closes it. Not derivable from source.",
  "power_fault / speed_gate": "UNKNOWN. A severe power fault degrades flight and could reduce ground speed below the 2 m/s threshold, but nothing in source links battery trust to commanded velocity. Physical plausibility, not source.",
  "unexpected_maneuver / speed_gate": "UNKNOWN. A manoeuvre is defined by unusual kinematics; whether it crosses below the speed threshold is scenario-dependent."
 },
